; Burrow — the memcomparable key codec. Pure OCaml (depends only on the in-memory Bson value type, no
; LMDB/C), so it lives cleanly on the pure side and is property-testable with no disk. The byte order
; of an encoded key equals Bson.compare's value order; encodings are prefix-free so index entries
; (key ++ _id) and compound keys concatenate correctly.
;
; Tests are INLINE (let%test at the bottom of key_codec.ml — the order-preservation law over 200k
; random pairs); native-only lib, so the registrations never reach a browser bundle.
(library
 (name burrow_codec)
 (public_name fennec-mongo.burrow.codec)
 (libraries fennec-mongo.bson fennec-hunt.unit)
 (inline_tests
  (backend fennec-hunt.runner))
 (preprocess
  (pps fennec-hunt.ppx)))
